ges. What should I do next?","native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"user","sequence":15,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T11:56:20.745306","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":15,"usage":{"completion_tokens":22,"prompt_tokens":2597}},{"content":"Let’s continue troubleshooting your MMS issue. Please follow these steps on your phone:\n\n1. Check if you have a good cellular signal and that mobile data is enabled.\n2. Make sure Airplane Mode is OFF.\n3. Confirm that you are not connected to a VPN.\n\nCould you please check your phone’s status bar and let me know:\n- If you see any signal bars,\n- If mobile data is enabled (look for 4G, 5G, LTE, etc.),\n- If Airplane Mode is on,\n- If you see a VPN icon.\n\nThis information will help me determine the next steps.","native_cost":0.0,"participant":"evaluated_agent","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"assistant","sequence":16,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T11:56:22.838001","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":16,"usage":{"completion_tokens":127,"prompt_tokens":7002}},{"content":null,"native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"user","sequence":17,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T11:56:23.638774","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[{"arguments":{},"id":"call_RcV65k4rWwdtOAlgUgSWVIrz","name":"check_status_bar","requestor":"user_simulator"}],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":17,"usage":{"completion_tokens":12,"prompt_tokens":2750}},{"content":"Status Bar: 📶¹ Poor | 2G | 📵 Data Disabled | 🔋 80%","native_cost":null,"participant":"tool_environment","reasoning":null,"requestor":"user_simulator","role":"tool","sequence":18,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T11:56:23.639220","tool_call_id":"call_RcV65k4rWwdtOAlgUgSWVIrz","tool_calls":[],"tool_error":false,"turn_index":18,"usage":null},{"content":"Looking at my phone’s status bar, I see that the signal is poor, it shows 2G, and mobile data is disabled. Airplane Mode is off, and I don’t see any VPN icon. What should I do next?","native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"user","sequence":19,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T11:56:24.755511","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":19,"usage":{"completion_tokens":51,"prompt_tokens":2790}},{"content":"Thank you for the details. Here’s what you should do next:\n\n1. Enable mobile data on your phone.\n2. Change your network mode to prefer 4G or 5G (since 2G is not suitable for MMS).\n\nPlease enable mobile data first, then let me know if you need instructions on how to change your network mode preference. Once both are set, try sending an MMS again and let me know the result.","native_cost":0.0,"participant":"evaluated_agent","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"assistant","sequence":20,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T11:56:27.288357","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":20,"usage":{"completion_tokens":91,"prompt_tokens":7184}},{"content":null,"native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"user","sequence":21,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T11:56:28.083630","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[{"arguments":{},"id":"call_d3K0icbLepHugnV1ipQ1gICZ","name":"toggle_data","requestor":"user_simulator"}],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":21,"usage":{"completion_tokens":11,"prompt_tokens":2936}},{"content":"Mobile Data is now ON.\nStatus Bar: 📶¹ Poor | 2G | 📱 Data Enabled | 🔋 80%","native_cost":null,"participant":"tool_environment","reasoning":null,"requestor":"user_simulator","role":"tool","sequence":22,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T11:56:28.084070","tool_call_id":"call_d3K0icbLepHugnV1ipQ1gICZ","tool_calls":[],"tool_error":false,"turn_index":22,"usage":null},{"content":"I’ve enabled mobile data, but my phone still shows 2G with a poor signal. Should I go ahead and change the network mode to prefer 4G or 5G now? If so, could you guide me through that?","native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"user","sequence":23,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T11:56:29.475115","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":23,"usage":{"completion_tokens":51,"prompt_tokens":2980}},{"content":"Yes, you should change your network mode to prefer 4G or 5G, as 2G is not suitable for sending MMS. Here’s how you can do it:\n\n1. Go to your phone’s Settings.\n2. Find the section for “Mobile Network” or “Cellular Network.”\n3. Look for “Network Mode” or “Preferred Network Type.”\n4. Select an option like “4G/5G preferred” or “LTE/4G/5G auto.”\n\nAfter you change the network mode, wait a moment for your phone to connect to a better network. Once you see 4G, LTE, or 5G in your status bar, try sending an MMS again.\n\nLet me know if you need more detailed steps for your specific phone model, or if you still have trouble after making this change.","native_cost":0.0,"participant":"evaluated_agent","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"assistant","sequence":24,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T11:56:32.528887","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":24,"usage":{"completion_tokens":173,"prompt_tokens":7330}},{"content":null,"native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"user","sequence":25,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T11:56:33.860763","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[{"arguments":{"mode":"4g_5g_preferred"},"id":"call_YytHX3xgvFaoytJV1s0h1Sbv","name":"set_network_mode_preference","requestor":"user_simulator"}],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":25,"usage":{"completion_tokens":24,"prompt_tokens":3208}},{"content":"Preferred Network Mode set to: 4g_5g_preferred\nStatus Bar: 📶⁴ Excellent | 5G | 📱 Data Enabled | 🔋 80%","native_cost":null,"participant":"tool_environment","reasoning":null,"requestor":"user_simulator","role":"tool","sequence":26,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T11:56:33.861214","tool_call_id":"call_YytHX3xgvFaoytJV1s0h1Sbv","tool_calls":[],"tool_error":false,"turn_index":26,"usage":null},{"content":null,"native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"user","sequence":27,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T11:56:35.267383","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[{"arguments":{},"id":"call_4CGStKyZNXDfmDjqiTDE83Bx","name":"can_send_mms","requestor":"user_simulator"}],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":27,"usage":{"completion_tokens":13,"prompt_tokens":3279}},{"content":"Your messaging app cannot send MMS messages.","native_cost":null,"participant":"tool_environment","reasoning":null,"requestor":"user_simulator","role":"tool","sequence":28,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T11:56:35.267754","tool_call_id":"call_4CGStKyZNXDfmDjqiTDE83Bx","tool_calls":[],"tool_error":false,"turn_index":28,"usage":null},{"content":"I changed the network mode to prefer 4G/5G, and now my phone shows an excellent 5G signal with mobile data enabled. However, I still can’t send MMS messages. What should I try next?","native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"user","sequence":29,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T11:56:36.736915","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":29,"usage":{"completion_tokens":48,"prompt_tokens":3307}},{"content":"Thank you for updating your network settings. The next step is to check your phone’s APN (Access Point Name) settings, as incorrect APN or missing MMSC URL can prevent MMS from working.\n\nPlease check your APN settings and let me know if you see an MMSC (Multimedia Messaging Service Center) URL listed. If you’re unsure how to check, I can guide you through the process. Would you like instructions o